      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report two cases whose right gastroepiploic arterial bypass grafts were protected by a dual blood supply due to the anatomical anastomosis between the celiac and the superior mesenteric artery systems. This unique characteristic of the graft adds an advantage for its use as a graft conduit."},
